      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-240510",
      ":question/problem": "In a triangle $\u25b3ABC$, $D$ is a point between $B$ and $C$ such that $AD^(\u2015)\u22a5BC^(\u2015)$, and $AB = AC$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> $BD^(\u2015)\u2245CD^(\u2015)$\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $\u2220ADB$ and $\u2220ADC$ are right angles | $AD^(\u2015)\u22a5BC^(\u2015)$ |\n| 2 | $\u25b3ADB$ and $\u25b3ADC$ are right triangles | Definition of a right triangle |\n| 3 | $AB = AC$ | Given |\n| 4 | $AB^(\u2015)\u2245AC^(\u2015)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 5 | $AD^(\u2015)\u2245AD^(\u2015)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 6 | $\u25b3ADB\u2245\u25b3ADC$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 7 | $BD^(\u2015)\u2245CD^(\u2015)$ | CPCTC |"
    },
