      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-241871",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/29/292177d40186a5a0073d4f0634931736493cab17e3537e983c32468e58c6ce4b.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $PQ^(\u2015)\u22a5RL^(\u2015)$ and $m\u2220PRL = m\u2220QRL$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> *The segments $PL^(\u2015)$ and $QL^(\u2015)$ are congruent.*\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $\u2220PLR$ and $\u2220QLR$ are right angles | $PQ^(\u2015)\u22a5RL^(\u2015)$ |\n| 2 | $\u2220PLR\u2245\u2220QLR$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 3 | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |\n| 4 | $m\u2220PRL = m\u2220QRL$ | Given |\n| 5 | $\u2220PRL\u2245\u2220QRL$ | Definition of congruent angles |\n| 6 | $\u25b3PRL\u2245\u25b3QRL$ | {{field-4}} |\n| 7 | $PL^(\u2015)\u2245QL^(\u2015)$ | CPCTC |"
    },
