      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-241904",
      ":question/problem": "In the triangle $\u25b3ABC$, $AD^(\u2015)$ is an altitude and $BD = CD$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> $\u2220ABD\u2245\u2220ACD$\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $BD = CD$ | Given |\n| 2 | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |\n| 3 | $AD^(\u2015)\u22a5BC^(\u2015)$ | Definition of an altitude |\n| 4 | $\u2220ADB$ and $\u2220ADC$ are right angles | $AD^(\u2015)\u22a5BC^(\u2015)$ |\n| 5 | $\u2220ADB\u2245\u2220ADC$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 6 | $AD^(\u2015)\u2245AD^(\u2015)$ | Reflexive property of congruence |\n| 7 | $\u25b3ABD\u2245\u25b3ACD$ | {{field-4}} |\n| 8 | $\u2220ABD\u2245\u2220ACD$ | CPCTC |"
    }
